#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edb95343-d14b-5c9d-a0f9-c4b57323a384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311106} {:answer/id #uuid "1ed5d913-6b6c-5367-8541-030232b01964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311107} {:answer/id #uuid "46105c4e-45f2-5924-bb5a-e89dd6113e0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311108} {:answer/id #uuid "1e8758bc-6709-57c9-9a62-d574605c3516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311109} {:answer/id #uuid "1871cc37-f619-5953-91eb-dcfa6e561709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ed5d913-6b6c-5367-8541-030232b01964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311107} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7d8119a-200e-536b-a008-1a1710b3a4d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aaf48b17-9dee-583c-9e29-c168f66ed80b" :question/math-academy-id "q-126458" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $C(-1,0,4)$ and $D(-7,2,11).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $C$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=c+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $c$ is the position vector of $C.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $C(-1,0,4)$ and $D(-7,2,11)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =⟨-7,2,11⟩-⟨-1,0,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,2,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6dee200-f517-5645-87ec-ccf36012e55e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Equation of the Line Passing Through Two Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c02a6cb-8517-54ec-b552-1e1a0689cda9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387165} {:answer/id #uuid "42f0a19a-07c9-50d9-9509-a712a1e685b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387166} {:answer/id #uuid "284b8741-4fde-5117-a4a6-c665c4ce6c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387167} {:answer/id #uuid "869bfa2a-6dcf-5505-871d-aa8c523516b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387168} {:answer/id #uuid "5544d965-eff4-5b3d-9f8f-bdda177aa80a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42f0a19a-07c9-50d9-9509-a712a1e685b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387166} :answer-field/id #uuid "aac6f2cb-01c6-5596-aa8e-cd099dd99144" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36087a77-de9c-54d4-8570-665799a1fd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-126744" :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the line that passes through the points $F(-5,-2,4)$ and $G(3,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $F$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=f+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $f$ is the position vector of $F.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $F(-5,-2,4)$ and $G(3,-1,1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{FG} \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,1⟩-⟨-5,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f78fe749-e37e-53f2-879f-4c36931c1d6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66342827-5cf6-5474-a1ba-b18b10cf0657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387172} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ae006f-c6a9-5627-9216-93223ef50594" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387173} {:answer/id #uuid "628e0ac7-80df-58b4-b9fa-7967af50269b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387174} {:answer/id #uuid "0a9efbb5-889d-5a01-a06f-edb9b9fe99f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387175} {:answer/id #uuid "6c3799d7-c7a4-5b2e-befb-8bdb8d9e6b2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2ae006f-c6a9-5627-9216-93223ef50594" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387173} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dc93760-d0b0-5810-85f8-61f6441f9783" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f673252d-f985-582f-b040-6f3a954cdf57" :question/math-academy-id "q-162161" :question/problem "The equation below describes all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(3,0,-2)$ and $Q(1,1,-1).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ b \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [c,1]\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand the vector equation of the  line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=3+1+0=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f78fe749-e37e-53f2-879f-4c36931c1d6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c629dade-033a-586a-86cb-9a3a28ab2c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311141} {:answer/id #uuid "5bba45e5-faf5-5659-93d3-53ec7bf78a45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311142} {:answer/id #uuid "9a730777-44f1-53e9-a66a-0de5f90d7a21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311143} {:answer/id #uuid "711bc41e-b8e6-5954-ab38-2933d27f8321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311144} {:answer/id #uuid "a315c075-de13-5d23-9919-27d8cb3fba4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c629dade-033a-586a-86cb-9a3a28ab2c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311141} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6a4c70d-05f1-57b6-b794-8282742733bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7a17e80-b445-5fbb-9914-628d51dd5f0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-162173" :question/problem "The equation below gives a parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(3,2,-1)$ and $Q(0,1,-3).$\n\n$$\nr(t)=a\\,i+b\\,j-(2t+1)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,c]\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(j-3\\,k)-(3\\,i+2\\,j-k) \\\\  & =-3\\,i-j-2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\nr=p+tv\\,⟹\\,r=(3\\,i+2\\,j-k)+t(-3\\,i-j-2\\,k)\n$$\n\nand the parametrization of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(3\\,i+2\\,j-k)+t(-3\\,i-j-2\\,k) \\\\  & =(3-3t)\\,i+(2-t)\\,j-(2t+1)\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,1].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=(3-3t)+(2-t)+1=6-4t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c338d1eb-7e13-5089-8dd3-d5ca6eefd4ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points on a Line That Are a Fixed Distance From Another Point on the Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f299e4ee-0d87-5b20-b9c2-616a468cd553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(10,18,8)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311210} {:answer/id #uuid "9b81aa93-84f4-569d-9611-f982ef89af8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(10,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311211} {:answer/id #uuid "fc89ac3c-5852-5b09-80a0-e4ce2ddea766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(8,-12,5)$ and ${A}_{2}(7,6,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311212} {:answer/id #uuid "a147f309-f3f8-50d0-bd0a-e3cf9539e610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311213} {:answer/id #uuid "bf60c65e-1a30-55f7-9f35-bf29135bc1bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(10,2,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(7,6,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a147f309-f3f8-50d0-bd0a-e3cf9539e610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311213} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee7d575-a0c4-5892-a256-694602bc0503" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f8ced46a-f7bf-550c-ae94-d64f15be9c59" :question/math-academy-id "q-77442" :question/problem "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(4,0,-1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨2,-6,3⟩.$ Find all the possible points $A$ on that line such that $PA=7.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $A$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OA} & =⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PA} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨4,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,-6,3⟩)-⟨4,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,⟨2,-6,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-6t,\\,3t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PA=7,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PA & =7 \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PA}| & =7 \\\\ |⟨2t,\\,-6t,\\,3t⟩| & =7 \\\\ \\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(-6t)^{2}+(3t)^{2}} & =7 \\\\ \\sqrt{49{t}^{2}} & =7 \\\\ \\pm 7t & =7 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 1$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{1}}=⟨4,0,-1⟩+⟨2,-6,3⟩=⟨6,-6,2⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{A}_{2}}=⟨4,0,-1⟩-⟨2,-6,3⟩=⟨2,6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${A}_{1}(6,-6,2)$ and ${A}_{2}(2,6,-4).$"}]}
